<title>FRANCE: Algeria buys 75,000 tonnes soft wheat - traders.</title>
<headline>Algeria buys 75,000 tonnes soft wheat - traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria has bought 75,000 tonnes of soft wheat at around $174-$175 per tonne, including cost and freight, European grain traders said.</p>
<p>The wheat is for shipment in April and May, they said.  </p>
<p>Traders said that the wheat was paid for in cash and was likely to come from France.</p>
<p>Algeria had launched a tender for the import of 75,000 tonnes of French or Argentine or U.S. wheat or any combination of the three.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
